{
  "version": 1,
  "description": "Canonical device shapes for marketing visuals: the website scenes (septena-site) and the App Store panels (appstore/). The iPad is drawn in landscape. Units are points (dp on Android) at 1x. A phone case is the screen plus the bezel on every side; screen radius = outerRadius - bezel. A laptop is a lid (a thin rim, a black glass bezel, the screen) on a base that overhangs the lid; outerRadius rounds the lid top, hingeRadius the lid bottom. corner: continuous (Apple) or circular. registry/device-shape.mjs draws these; renderers never redefine them. system names the OS a frame's screen must look like (docs/PLATFORM_CHROME.md): os and version are the target release, icons the column of registry/icons.json the app's own glyphs come from (sf = sfSymbol, material = material; the Windows client is planned on Compose Desktop, so Material), chrome the renderer's system chrome id, chrome the renderer's system chrome id.",
